# CURSOR lane

Cursor is one lane on a hub-and-spoke board. The other lanes (SPINE in Claude.ai;
CC-BUILD, CC-QUERY, CC-POSITIONS, CC-ABACUS in Claude Code) are described in
`docs/handoffs/lanes/README.md`. That file, `PROJECT_RULES.md`, and `CLAUDE.md` bind
this lane the same as every other.

## Session start (do these before any work)

1. `git fetch origin` and state the SHA of `origin/main` you are reading.
2. Read `docs/handoffs/lanes/*.md` — every lane's status file, newest first. This is
   the cross-environment memory that travels with the repo.
3. Read `C:\Users\nickh\.claude\projects\C--trading-hub\memory\MEMORY.md` (the Claude
   Code lanes' local memory index). Follow links into it only for the area you are
   about to touch. It is outside the repo on purpose — it may hold book figures.
4. If the task touches code another lane owns (see README ownership table), stop and
   say so; the fix is a relay to that lane, not an edit.

## Session end

- Rewrite `docs/handoffs/lanes/CURSOR.md` (whole-file rewrite, not append): what
  changed, what is in flight, what the next session should do first, and the SHA you
  worked against. Public-safe only — no balances, positions, P&L, routes, credentials.
- If you learned something durable that the Claude Code lanes need (a landmine, a
  ruling, a corrected assumption), write it as a new file in the memory directory
  above using the same frontmatter shape as its neighbours, and add one index line to
  `MEMORY.md`. That directory is the only channel that reaches those lanes without a
  git commit.

## Where this lane works

- **Worktree, not the shared checkout.** `C:\trading-hub` is sync-and-package only
  (SPINE ruling 2026-07-24). Build in `C:\th-cursor` (branch `cursor/<topic>`), or a
  fresh `git worktree add`. Never commit from `C:\trading-hub`.
- **Branch + PR, never a direct push to `main`.** A push to `main` is a Railway
  production deploy. Open a PR; Nick or the owning lane merges.
- **Stage by pathspec** (`git add <file> <file>`), never `-A`/`.`/`-a`. Run a
  credential pattern scan on the exact paths before staging; report counts, never values.
- **Never `git checkout --`, `stash`, `reset`, or `clean` a diff you did not create** —
  in any worktree. A dirty tree is another lane, live.

## Data access

- Hub data: the `pandora-hub` MCP (read-only, GitHub OAuth). Call `mcp_ping` first.
  Tool names are `hub_get_*`; the Olympus skills expect exactly these.
- Direct DB: the `postgres` MCP is read-only by construction. Writes to the book belong
  to CC-POSITIONS — never write to `unified_positions`, `position_lots`,
  `position_legs`, or `trades` from this lane.
- `scripts/reconcile_rh.py` is under a standing DO-NOT-RUN (`PROJECT_RULES.md`).

## Skills

The Olympus (TORO, URSA, PYTHIA, PYTHAGORAS, DAEDALUS, THALES, PIVOT) and Titans
(ATLAS, HELIOS, AEGIS, ATHENA) skills are junctioned from `skills/<agent>/` in this
repo into `~/.cursor/skills/`. Source of truth is the repo copy. A `_shared/...`
reference inside a skill resolves to `skills/_shared/`. Do not edit skills from this
lane without saying so on the face of `CURSOR.md` — the packaged Claude.ai bundles
are regenerated from these files.
